flowchart TB
    accTitle: The rerun of a run that failed
    accDescr: A message names a run of GitHub Actions that failed on main: that of a workflow, or an entry of the alarm, such as a release. Dennis presses Rerun, and the pager reads the run. While it still runs, or once it passed on a retry, the button says so and nothing starts. Otherwise its failed jobs run again, and the message says so. When they fail again, the message shows the failure, and Rerun can run them once more. When they pass, the workflow turns green, or the entry goes, and the last one turns the alarm green.

    alarm["`**🚨** A message names a run that failed on main: a workflow, or an entry of the alarm`"]
    press["Dennis presses 🔁 Rerun"]
    read["The pager reads the run"]
    nothing["`**ℹ️** It still runs, or passed on a retry: the button says so, and nothing starts`"]
    again["`**🔁** Its failed jobs run again, and the message says so`"]
    green["`**✅** They pass: the workflow turns green, or the entry goes, and the last one turns the alarm green`"]

    alarm --> press --> read
    read -- "still running, or green" --> nothing
    read -- "failed" --> again
    again -- "they fail again: the message shows the failure" --> alarm
    again -- "a pass" --> green

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef warn fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class press you
    class read,nothing,again bot
    class green done
    class alarm warn
